==Trivia==
*His Japanese name, Hakate Tarō, is likely a reference to violinist and composer [[wikipedia:Taro Hakase|Taro Hakase]], or Hakase Tarō as he's called in Japanese. It's also a play on words, as Hakate is spelled with the kanji for "grave" (墓) and "hand" or "arm" (手).
*His attack animation is ''[[wikipedia:Kanchō|kanchō]]'', a Japanese prank which involves using one's fingers to poke the target from behind. Most units don't face the right direction for it to work, but [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]] isn't so lucky.
*His backswing animation is a reference to the movie ''[[wikipedia:Terminator 2: Judgement Day|Terminator 2: Judgement Day]]'', where the T-800 Terminator gives a thumbs up before sinking into molten metal.
*When knocked back, his hands do the "[https://natalie.mu/comic/news/159046 Chudōn Pose]" (ちゅどーんポーズ), a gag pose found in works by [[wikipedia:Rumiko Takahashi|Rumiko Takahashi]] such as ''[[Ranma 1/2 Collaboration Event|Ranma 1/2]]''.
*His Japanese description says that he is a ''jibakurei'' (地縛霊), meaning a ghost who can't leave a specific location. In this case, it would presumably be his grave.
*He is apparently [[Miss Haka]]'s husband. Their Japanese names share the surname Hakate (墓手), and Lord Gravey's Japanese description mentions that he was accused of sexual harassment, while Miss Haka's says her husband was taken in for that same reason.
*If counting him as an [[Empire of Cats]] enemy, then he and Miss Haka are the only ones to have no variants.

